    description: "Taking a focus break specifically in or looking at nature to replenish depleted top-down attention (Attention Restoration Theory). In two experiments, a walk in nature — or even viewing nature images — improved directed-attention measures (backward digit span, Attention Network Task) more than an urban equivalent (Berman, Jonides & Kaplan 2008).",
