    impact: { magnitude: 4, latency: "days", durability: "lasting", effort: "moderate" },
    feeds: ["consistent recurring judgments", "reducing noise", "predictive accuracy", "resisting halo and impression effects"],
    description: "For recurring judgments, combine the relevant cues with a simple explicit rule (a checklist score, weighted-additive model, even equal weights) rather than integrating them 'in your head'. Grove & Meehl's meta-analysis of 136 studies found mechanical prediction equaled or beat clinical judgment ~90% of the time (about 10% more accurate on average). Dawes showed even improper equal-weight linear models routinely outperform expert intuition, largely by eliminating human inconsistency (noise).",
