    description: "Persuading through a story that 'transports' the audience - absorbing them into the narrative world - shifts beliefs, attitudes, and intentions more than argument alone in many contexts. A meta-analysis of 132 effect sizes from 76 articles found narrative transportation reliably predicts persuasion, with transportation increased by identifiable characters, imagery, and low prior familiarity (Van Laer et al., 2014). The effect is real but medium-sized and moderated heavily by audience and medium.",
