    description: "When work is experienced as pointless — the inverse of meaningful work — engagement, commitment, and satisfaction collapse and withdrawal follows. A meta-analysis of 44 studies (N ≈ 23,144) found meaningful work correlates strongly (r ≈ .70+) with work engagement, commitment, and job satisfaction, and moderately with life satisfaction, health, and (negatively) withdrawal intentions. Absence of meaning is thus a powerful drag on motivation, performance, and broader well-being, not just a workplace mood.",
