    description: "In the Bureau of Justice Statistics' Victims of Identity Theft series, most incidents are resolved with modest direct cost (median ~$160 out-of-pocket; median ~2 hours), but a long tail of unresolved cases drags on for weeks and correlates with sustained distress. In a nationally representative sample of 2,000+ victims aged 65+, roughly a third rated the experience moderately-to-severely distressing even when out-of-pocket loss was zero — the harm is emotional and administrative as much as financial. Longer misuse windows, follow-on financial problems, and hours spent resolving each independently predict more emotional consequences (worry, anger, feeling violated/unsafe).",
