    evidenceTag: "Moderate",
    harm: { severity: 3, onset: "months", reversibility: "recovers" },
    degrades: ["Physical recovery and health", "Long-term productivity", "Cognitive performance", "Immune function"],
    description: "Presenteeism — attending work while ill — trades short-term attendance for long-term damage. A systematic review (Skagen & Collins, 2016) found sickness presenteeism at baseline predicts future sickness absence and worse self-rated health over time. A meta-analysis of 109 samples (N~176,000; Miraglia & Johns, 2016) shows presenteeism is driven by ill health under high demands, strict absence constraints, and job insecurity, and paradoxically also by high engagement.",
