    description: "Early-life lead exposure produces measurable, largely irreversible cognitive loss. Lanphear et al.'s (2005) international pooled analysis of seven prospective cohorts found that a rise in concurrent blood lead from 2.4 to 30 ug/dL was associated with a ~6.9-point Full-Scale IQ decrement, with a steeper (supralinear) effect at the lowest levels -- meaning no safe threshold. The lead-IQ function underpins EPA lifetime-earnings loss estimates. Effects manifest as lower IQ, worse attention, and reduced academic attainment.",
